auth {
  mode: none
}

docs {
  # Vida Verde API

  Backend for the Vida Verde Spanish school platform (Phase 1).

  ## URL prefixes -- one per audience

  | Prefix | Who | Auth |
  |---|---|---|
  | `/public/` | marketing site visitors | none |
  | `/student/` | logged-in students | Bearer `{{accessTokenStudent}}` |
  | `/administrator/` | school staff | Bearer `{{accessTokenAdmin}}` |
  | `/teacher/` | teachers | reserved for Phase 2 -- no endpoints yet |
  | `/rest-auth/` | login, logout, password | mixed |

  ## Getting a token

  Run **authentication > login**. Its post-response script stores the access
  token in `accessTokenAdmin` or `accessTokenStudent` depending on the role
  the API returns, so every other request picks it up automatically.

  Seed logins (`python manage.py seed_demo`):

  - master admin -- `master@vidaverde.test` / `vidaverde123`
  - manager -- `manager@vidaverde.test` / `vidaverde123`
  - student -- `ana.lopez@example.com` / `student123`

  ## Response shape

  Writes and errors return `{"success": true|false, ...}`. Errors are flattened
  by `administrator.serializers.custom_exception_handler` into
  `{"success": false, "message": "(field) explanation"}`.

  List endpoints that paginate use `?p=<page>&page_size=<n>`.
}
